SUMMARY:WUNC Spotlight: From Mic to Medicine: Inside 49 Years of "The People's Pharmacy"
DESCRIPTION:Go behind the scenes of “The People’s Pharmacy\,” one of public radio’s longest-running health programs. Join hosts Joe and Terry Graedon for an interactive conversation featuring memorable audio moments\, stories from the show’s history\, and an inside look at how episodes are created—from choosing topics and booking guests to navigating live broadcasts and making editorial decisions. You’ll even help explore how a future episode could come together. Whether you’re a longtime listener or simply curious about health journalism\, you’ll leave with new insights and practical takeaways.\nComplimentary lunch provided. Space is limited; advance registration is encouraged.\nThis event is part of WUNC’s 50th anniversary celebration\, featuring 50 events across North Carolina that bring people together through community\, conversation\, and storytelling.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/wunc-spotlight-from-mic-to-medicine-inside-49-years-of-the-peoples-pharmacy/
LOCATION:WUNC Public Radio Suite 600\, 324 Blackwell st. Suite 600\, Durham\, 27701
CATEGORIES:Community Engagement,Free,Health,Science & Technology
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/4_Option-1-1.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="WUNC Public Radio":MAILTO:events@wunc.org
